{"agent":"codex-agent","artifact_sha256":"088ad8b5560c8e97a9280c39710d2d8183f8d003b2644483c534522bd4c29de9","assumptions":["The gated decision concerns acceptance of the VERIFY run and its evidence, not a claim that the overall delivery goal is complete; the artifact explicitly records goal_complete=false.","The per-check status, exit, and duration fields are intended to represent the final-baseline execution named by the artifact.","Referenced evidence files were not independently inspected because the review instructions permit reading only the supplied artifact."],"confidence":0.91,"findings":[{"blocking":true,"claim":"A required check is classified as PASS even though its sole structured execution result is a failure, making the PASS tally and P1-07 final readback internally inconsistent.","evidence":"The V_RW_COMPLETION_REQUIRED entry has required=true, status=\"PASS\", exit=1, and seconds=8. Its note says the initial run failed and a later run reached 12/12 after index regeneration, but no separate final attempt, exit=0 result, or final-baseline execution record is represented. The P1-07 final_readback nevertheless cites it as green.","id":"FINAL-RESULT-001","recommendation":"Record initial and final attempts separately, including baseline identity, command, exit code, duration, and evidence for the asserted 12/12 rerun; then regenerate the tally and all final reports.","severity":"BLOCKER"},{"blocking":true,"claim":"Two required journey checks are marked PASS without structured execution outcomes, contradicting the assertion that all 118 required checks were executed at the final baseline.","evidence":"V_RW_REAL_COMET_RECOVERY and V_POST_DELIVERY_PERMISSIONS each have required=true and status=\"PASS\" but both exit and seconds are null. The artifact simultaneously reports checks_total=118 and tally.not_executed=0. Narrative recipe_check and journey descriptions do not reconcile the missing command outcomes.","id":"FINAL-RESULT-002","recommendation":"Attach immutable final-baseline attempt records with non-null outcomes and timing for both commands, or classify them as unverified/not executed and recompute the tally.","severity":"BLOCKER"},{"blocking":false,"claim":"The P1-05 binding labels real Runner isolation as qualified while its real-container portion remains explicitly unverified.","evidence":"P1-05 states claim=\"real Runner isolation qualification\", but its fix_commits describe only the \"I02 local half\" and its final_readback says \"real-container S6/S7/S8 remain staged-UNVERIFIED\". The unverified ledger assigns I02_REAL_CONTAINER_S6_S7_S8 to I01 refs admission/runtime admission.","id":"CLOSURE-SCOPE-003","recommendation":"Rename the binding as local build/admission qualification and keep P1-05 open, or execute and record the S6/S7/S8 real-container probes before claiming full qualification.","severity":"MAJOR"},{"blocking":false,"claim":"The report usefully preserves unresolved scope instead of declaring the overall goal complete.","evidence":"The top-level goal_complete is false; the tally separately reports 104 PASS, 9 known environment drift, 3 UNVERIFIED, and 2 failed; the unverified_ledger names holders for outstanding capabilities.","id":"HONESTY-004","recommendation":"Preserve this explicit goal state and holder ledger when regenerating the corrected final evidence.","severity":"NOTE"}],"review_id":"rework-verify-final-20261023","round":0,"score":{"criteria":{"actionability":8.4,"completeness":6.3,"correctness":6.0,"evidence":5.8,"risk":5.9},"overall":6.2},"summary":"REJECT the current final evidence package. The honest incomplete-goal disposition is valuable, but the machine-readable final-baseline record contradicts itself: one PASS retains exit 1 without a recorded successful rerun, and two required PASS journeys have null execution outcomes. These defects must be reconciled before the VERIFY node and run completion can be authorized.","verdict":"REJECT"}

